$ node scripts/rea.mjs inspect-deb-package --help
rea inspect-deb-package — Inspect a local Debian .deb without installing it or running maintainer scripts

Usage: rea inspect-deb-package <path> [options]

Arguments:
  path  Local Debian .deb package

Options:
  --max-file-bytes <value>       Maximum stable artifact bytes to read (default 64 MiB) (default: 67108864)
  --max-ar-members <value>       Maximum ar members to inventory (default 32) (default: 32)
  --max-control-entries <value>  Maximum control.tar entries to inventory (default 4096) (default: 4096)
  --max-data-entries <value>     Maximum data.tar entries to inventory (default 4096) (default: 4096)
  --max-control-bytes <value>    Maximum decompressed control.tar bytes (default 1 MiB) (default: 1048576)
  --max-data-bytes <value>       Maximum decompressed data.tar bytes (default 32 MiB) (default: 33554432)

Custom Global Options:
  --timings  Write measured command timing to stderr.

Global Options:
  --filter-output <keys>              Filter output by key paths (e.g. foo,bar.baz,a[0,3])
  --format <toon|json|yaml|md|jsonl>  Output format
  --full-output                       Show full output envelope
  --help                              Show help
  --llms, --llms-full                 Print LLM-readable manifest
  --schema                            Show JSON Schema for command
  --token-count                       Print token count of output (instead of output)
  --token-limit <n>                   Limit output to n tokens
  --token-offset <n>                  Skip first n tokens of output
exit 0

